I see the vulnerability now. In `render_attribute`, there's a loop:
```c
for(i = 0; attr->substr_offsets[i] < attr->size; i++) {
    MD_TEXTTYPE type = attr->substr_types[i];
    MD_OFFSET off = attr->substr_offsets[i];
    MD_SIZE size = attr->substr_offsets[i+1] - off;
```

The loop condition checks `attr->substr_offsets[i] < attr->size`, but then accesses `attr->substr_types[i]` and `attr->substr_offsets[i+1]`. If `substr_offsets[i]` is the last element and equals `attr->size`, the loop exits. But if `substr_offsets[i] < attr->size` for the last element, then `substr_offsets[i+1]` is out of bounds. This is a buffer overflow reading beyond the array.

Let me look at the `md4c.c` source to understand how `substr_offsets` is built and where the actual overflow occurs. Let me search for relevant code.

